Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:12:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): big Fusion Lab mark on the workshop hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The workshop hero (LabHero — "Fusion lab · с. Минай...") had nothing
above the eyebrow line: no logo, no badge, just page background. The
owner asked for the marketplace's own big mark there — same source crop
process as the header mark (30c324d), just without the 9×9 header
constraint, so it stands as a section mark of its own rather than a nav
icon.

apps/web/public/fusion-lab-mark-hero.png — cropped to opaque bounds
(alpha threshold 30, stable 10-200) with a 6% pad, 640px on the long
side. Plain <img>, matching the header's own convention.

Verified: next typegen + tsc --noEmit clean. Full `next build` fails in
this sandbox on fetching Google Fonts (network egress, not a code
issue) — Vercel's own network reaches fonts.googleapis.com fine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
